{"episode_id": "7f618b986b50", "t": 1792140783.6298182, "step": 36, "to": 11, "kind": "bug", "hint_index": 3, "subtask_id": "dayjs-b24c255c0b29", "question_id": null, "text": "Fixed. Root cause: `src/plugin/weekYear/index.js` only handled the \"December in week 1 → next year\" case and never the symmetric \"January in week 52/53 → previous year\" case, which is what `yearStart: 4` (ISO-like week numbering) needs. Added the missing check; the reconstructed `yearStart: 4` test now passes and the full suite (56 suites / 524 tests, all timezone variants) is green.", "eta_min": 0.0, "done": true, "item": null, "subtask_ids": ["dayjs-b24c255c0b29"]}
{"episode_id": "7f618b986b50", "t": 1792140821.956125, "step": 38, "to": 15, "kind": "bug", "hint_index": 4, "subtask_id": "dayjs-3a929ee0ab06", "question_id": null, "text": "Got it — fifth bug, in customParseFormat (`meridiem locale AM` / `meridiem locale PM`). ETA ~12 min.", "eta_min": 12.0, "done": false, "item": null, "subtask_ids": ["dayjs-3a929ee0ab06"]}
{"episode_id": "7f618b986b50", "t": 1792140827.653182, "step": 39, "to": 1, "kind": "bug", "hint_index": 0, "subtask_id": "dayjs-f9d6b109fbdf", "question_id": null, "text": "Fixed. Root cause: `d.tz(input, timezone)` treated every input as a local wall-clock string (`d.utc(input)` + `fixOffset`), so numeric timestamps, JS `Date`s and Day.js objects got shifted by the zone offset instead of converted. Non-string inputs are now routed through the instant-preserving `d(input).tz(timezone)` path. Reconstructed `Parse parse timestamp, js Date, Day.js object` passes, and the full suite (56 suites / 524 tests) is green.", "eta_min": 0.0, "done": true, "item": null, "subtask_ids": ["dayjs-f9d6b109fbdf"]}
